   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Executive Summary: Assessing Upskilling Program Lift Under Positivity Violations\n",
    "\n",
    "### The Business Dilemma\n",
    "An enterprise tech firm launched an **Advanced Cloud Certification Program**. HR leadership observed that employees holding this certification earn **~$32,000 higher annual salaries** than non-certified peers. Eager to boost compensation parity and retention, executives want to mandate this certification across all talent tiers, including entry-level/junior engineers.\n",
    "\n",
    "However, historical company policy prohibited employees with fewer than 2 years of tenure from enrolling in the program: \n",
    "> **Entry Policy**: $P(\\text{Certification} \\mid \\text{Tenure} < 2\\text{ yrs}) = 0$\n",
    "\n",
    "### The Causal Trap\n",
    "When a subgroup has a zero probability of receiving treatment, the **Positivity Assumption** (a core pillar of causal inference) is strictly violated. Observational models cannot adjust for baseline differences where counterfactual data simply does not exist. Attempting to project earnings lift onto junior employees without accounting for positivity breakdown risks wasting enterprise budget on mandating programs that may yield drastically lower returns than estimated.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Project Objective\n",
    "1. **Simulate** employee profile data under realistic organizational entry controls.\n",
    "2. **Diagnose** positivity violations programmatically using propensity scores and cross-tabulations.\n",
    "3. **Demonstrate** why standard adjustment methods fail in zero-support regions.\n",
    "4. **Deliver** actionable guidance on where causal claims hold and where targeted pilot experiments are required."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Setup environment and set random seeds for full reproducibility\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "# Global settings\n",
    "NP_SEED = 101\n",
    "np.random.seed(NP_SEED)\n",
    "\n",
    "sns.set_theme(style=\"whitegrid\", palette=\"deep\")\n",
    "plt.rcParams[\"figure.figsize\"] = (10, 6)\n",
    "plt.rcParams[\"font.size\"] = 11\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Environment initialized successfully with seed:\", NP_SEED)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## Structural Causal Framework & The Positivity Assumption\n",
    "\n",
    "In causal inference, identifying the **Average Treatment Effect (ATE)** requires three identification conditions:\n",
    "1. **Exchangeability (Unconfoundedness)**: $Y(0), Y(1) \\perp T \\mid S$\n",
    "2. **Consistency**: $Y = Y(1) \\cdot T + Y(0) \\cdot (1 - T)$\n",
    "3. **Positivity (Overlap)**: $0 < P(T = 1 \\mid S = s) < 1 \\quad \\forall s \\text{ where } P(S = s) > 0$\n",
    "\n",
    "If $P(T = 1 \\mid S = s) = 0$ for a segment $s$, we have **zero empirical support**. We never observe $Y(1)$ for that group, making counterfactual reasoning impossible without parametric extrapolation assumptions.\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "   [ Experience / Tenure Tier (S) ] (Confounder)\n",
    "            /              \\\n",
    "           /                \\\n",
    "  (Strict Policy)            v\n",
    "          v           [ Salary Level (Y) ]\n",
    " [ Certification (T) ] ---------> (Outcome)\n",
    "    (Treatment)         True Lift\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def generate_employee_dataset(n_samples: int = 10000) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Simulates enterprise employee records with strict tenure-based enrollment rules.\n",
    "    \n",
    "    Ground Truth Rules:\n",
    "    - Confounder S: Tenure Tier\n",
    "        * Tier 0: Junior (< 2 yrs tenure) -> 35% of company\n",
    "        * Tier 1: Mid-level (2-5 yrs tenure) -> 40% of company\n",
    "        * Tier 2: Senior (5+ yrs tenure) -> 25% of company\n",
    "        \n",
    "    - Treatment T: Certification Status (0 = No, 1 = Yes)\n",
    "        * Junior (<2 yrs): Strict ZERO enrollment policy -> P(T=1) = 0.00 (Positivity Violation!)\n",
    "        * Mid-level (2-5 yrs): P(T=1) = 0.40\n",
    "        * Senior (5+ yrs): P(T=1) = 0.75\n",
    "        \n",
    "    - Outcome Y: Salary ($k USD)\n",
    "        * Baseline Salary by Tier: Junior = $65k, Mid = $95k, Senior = $135k\n",
    "        * True Causal Lift of Certification = +$12k (Constant across all tiers)\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    # 1. Simulate Confounder: Tenure Tier\n",
    "    tenure_tier = np.random.choice([0, 1, 2], size=n_samples, p=[0.35, 0.40, 0.25])\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # 2. Assign Treatment based on policy rules\n",
    "    prob_cert = np.zeros(n_samples)\n",
    "    prob_cert[tenure_tier == 1] = 0.40\n",
    "    prob_cert[tenure_tier == 2] = 0.75\n",
    "    # Note: tenure_tier == 0 remains 0.0 (Strict zero)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    treatment = np.random.binomial(n=1, p=prob_cert, size=n_samples)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # 3. Simulate Salary Outcome\n",
    "    base_salary = np.where(\n",
    "        tenure_tier == 0, 65.0,\n",
    "        np.where(tenure_tier == 1, 95.0, 135.0)\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    \n",
    "    noise = np.random.normal(loc=0.0, scale=6.0, size=n_samples)\n",
    "    true_cert_lift = 12.0 * treatment\n",
    "    \n",
    "    salary = base_salary + true_cert_lift + noise\n",
    "    \n",
    "    tier_labels = {0: 'Junior (<2 yrs)', 1: 'Mid-Level (2-5 yrs)', 2: 'Senior (5+ yrs)'}\n",
    "    \n",
    "    df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "        'employee_id': np.arange(1000, 1000 + n_samples),\n",
    "        'tenure_tier_code': tenure_tier,\n",
    "        'tenure_tier': [tier_labels[t] for t in tenure_tier],\n",
    "        'certified': treatment,\n",
    "        'salary_k': salary\n",
    "    })\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return df\n",
    "\n",
    "# Run simulation\n",
    "df_emp = generate_employee_dataset(n_samples=10000)\n",
    "df_emp.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## Step 1: Naive Observational Analysis"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Naive evaluation comparing certified vs non-certified employees\n",
    "naive_stats = df_emp.groupby('certified')['salary_k'].agg(['count', 'mean', 'std']).reset_index()\n",
    "naive_stats['certified_label'] = np.where(naive_stats['certified'] == 1, 'Certified', 'Non-Certified')\n",
    "\n",
    "non_cert_mean = naive_stats.loc[naive_stats['certified'] == 0, 'mean'].values[0]\n",
    "cert_mean = naive_stats.loc[naive_stats['certified'] == 1, 'mean'].values[0]\n",
    "naive_lift = cert_mean - non_cert_mean\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=== NAIVE SALARY METRICS ===\")
    "print(f\"Non-Certified Average Salary: ${non_cert_mean:.2f}k\")\n",
    "print(f\"Certified Average Salary:     ${cert_mean:.2f}k\")\n",
    "print(f\"Naive Observed Salary Lift:   +${naive_lift:.2f}k\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### The Executive Misinterpretation\n",
    "Looking only at the naive metric, HR concludes that cloud certification adds **+$32,000+** in employee value! They plan to mandate this training company-wide, expecting massive salary/productivity growth. However, this conflates senior tenure salary rates with certification impact."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## Step 2: Diagnostic Verification of Positivity Breakdown"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Cross-tabulation matrix to inspect exposure probability P(T=1 | S=s)\n",
    "positivity_matrix = pd.crosstab(\n",
    "    df_emp['tenure_tier'], \n",
    "    df_emp['certified'], \n",
    "    normalize='index'\n",
    ") * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "positivity_matrix.columns = ['% Non-Certified (T=0)', '% Certified (T=1)']\n",
    "print(\"=== POSITIVITY DIAGNOSTIC MATRIX (% Exposure by Group) ===\")\n",
    "print(positivity_matrix.round(2))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Heatmap Visualization of Treatment Probabilities\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 4))\n",
    "sns.heatmap(positivity_matrix, annot=True, fmt=\".1f\", cmap=\"YlOrRd\", cbar=True, vmin=0, vmax=100)\n",
    "plt.title(\"Positivity Diagnostic: Spotting Zero-Support Cells\", fontsize=13, fontweight='bold', pad=12)\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Tenure Tier\", fontsize=11)\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Treatment Status\", fontsize=11)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Diagnostic Findings\n",
    "Notice the top row: **Junior (<2 yrs)** employees have **0.0%** exposure to the treatment condition. \n",
    "* $P(T = 1 \\mid \\text{Junior}) = 0$\n",
    "* **Structural Zero**: The positivity assumption is completely violated for this stratum!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## Step 3: Stratified Analysis & Identification of Valid Support"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Compute conditional treatment effects within overlapping strata\n",
    "strat_summary = df_emp.groupby(['tenure_tier', 'certified'])['salary_k'].agg(['count', 'mean']).reset_index()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Pivot table for stratum-specific comparisons\n",
    "pivot_strat = strat_summary.pivot(index='tenure_tier', columns='certified', values='mean')\n",
    "pivot_strat.columns = ['Mean_Salary_Uncertified', 'Mean_Salary_Certified']\n",
    "pivot_strat['Observed_Stratum_Lift'] = pivot_strat['Mean_Salary_Certified'] - pivot_strat['Mean_Salary_Uncertified']\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=== STRATIFIED CAUSAL ESTIMATES ===\")\n",
    "print(pivot_strat.round(2))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plotting distribution of salary across tiers\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
    "sns.boxplot(\n",
    "    data=df_emp, \n",
    "    x='tenure_tier', \n",
    "    y='salary_k', \n",
    "    hue='certified', \n",
    "    palette=['#5B9BD5', '#ED7D31'],\n",
    "    ax=ax\n",
    ")\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"Salary Distribution by Tenure & Certification: Identifying Support Boundaries\", fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"Tenure Segment\", fontsize=11)\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"Salary ($k USD)\", fontsize=11)\n",
    "ax.legend(title=\"Certification Status\", labels=['Uncertified (T=0)', 'Certified (T=1)'])\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## Step 4: Computing Causal Impact On Common Support Region"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Filter dataset to Common Support Region (Mid-Level & Senior staff only)\n",
    "df_support = df_emp[df_emp['tenure_tier_code'] > 0].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Calculate weights relative to the overlap population\n",
    "tier_weights = df_support['tenure_tier'].value_counts(normalize=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Stratified ATE calculation on common support\n",
    "lift_mid = pivot_strat.loc['Mid-Level (2-5 yrs)', 'Observed_Stratum_Lift']\n",
    "lift_senior = pivot_strat.loc['Senior (5+ yrs)', 'Observed_Stratum_Lift']\n",
    "\n",
    "valid_ate = (lift_mid * tier_weights['Mid-Level (2-5 yrs)']) + (lift_senior * tier_weights['Senior (5+ yrs)'])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=== FINAL CAUSAL LIFT REPORT ===\")\n",
    "print(f\"Naive Unadjusted Estimate:              +${naive_lift:.2f}k\")\n",
    "print(f\"Valid Causal ATE (Common Support):      +${valid_ate:.2f}k\")\n",
    "print(f\"Ground-Truth Causal Effect Parameter:    +$12.00k\")\n",
    "print(\"\\nDecision Action: Restrict causal claims to 2+ year tenure staff; launch controlled pilot for Junior staff.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## Strategic Decision Matrix & ROI Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "| Analysis Approach | Estimated Salary Lift | Flaw / Risk | Executive Recommendation |\n",
    "| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n",
    "| **Naive Observational** | **+$32.10k** | Confounders + Positivity Breakdown | Mandate company-wide immediately (Flawed). |\n",
    "| **Positivity-Aware Causal Engine** | **+$12.02k** | Subpopulation bounded | Roll out to 2+ yr staff; run Pilot for Juniors. |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Financial Impact\n",
    "- **Budget Optimization**: Prevents projecting unrealistic +$32k salary benchmarks onto junior staff onboarding.\n",
    "- **Resource Preservation**: Saves $100k+ in unvalidated training expenses by targeting rollout to eligible cohorts first."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## Simulation Assumptions & Technical Limitations\n",
    "\n",
    "### Assumptions\n",
    "1. **Unconfoundedness in Support Region**: Assumes tenure tier is the sole major confounder for mid/senior staff salary differentials.\n",
    "2. **Constant Effect Model**: Simulated causal lift was modeled as an additive +$12k across tiers.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Limitations & Next Steps\n",
    "1. **Extrapolation Danger**: Machine learning models (e.g., Random Forests, XGBoost) trained on this data might output predictions for junior staff, but those estimates would be pure structural extrapolation.\n",
    "2. **Experimental Pilot Requirement**: To accurately measure the effect of certification on junior staff ($<2$ yrs), HR must run a **Randomized Pilot Trial** granting a subset of junior engineers entry into the program."
   ]
  }
